When inputs are partitioned by repeated separator rows or columns but demos produce much smaller outputs, dimension ratios help identify possible structure but do not establish the encoding. Keep distinct hypotheses for (a) summarizing interior regions, (b) recording separator/boundary markers at their intersections, and (c) selecting only rows or columns with special markers. For each demo, write down the exact partition counts and map candidate input coordinates or blocks to each output cell, including ordering. Reproduce every output exactly before transferring the map.

After an incorrect compact-output submission, do not merely alter colors or copy another visually salient set of markers. Reopen the task class and output representation, and re-derive dimensions and correspondence from all demos. Repeated, heterogeneous demos may share only an abstract structure; spend another demo only when two explicit mappings predict a materially different discriminating observation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792484434/attempts/a51726d22484491ca3bb302d2d403d60/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-task-delta-inference/references/compact-output-reassessment-after-errors.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-task-delta-inference", "file": "references/demo-output-mapping.md", "content": "# Validate the demo's output mapping before transfer

A visually structured demo output is not evidence by itself for reflection, tiling, or stamping. After the first plausible but incorrect submission, reopen the task class and output representation before changing coordinates. Record input/output dimensions, map input rows, columns, objects, or symbols to output cells/regions, and compare that candidate mapping against every available pair. Treat exact full-demo reproduction as a prerequisite for submitting; a coherent pattern that fails even one demo is still an unvalidated guess. If requesting another demo, identify which competing mappings its predicted output would distinguish.
